p><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="26" name="Text 22"/><p:cNvSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="6309360" y="4389120"/><a:ext cx="5120640" cy="1005840"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" lIns="0" tIns="0" rIns="0" bIns="0" rtlCol="0" anchor="ctr"/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPts val="1782"/></a:lnSpc><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1100" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="555D66"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Arial" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Arial" pitchFamily="34" charset="-122"/><a:cs typeface="Arial" pitchFamily="34" charset="-120"/></a:rPr><a:t>The whole account is one Performance Max campaign on a $50 daily budget, with the Business Profile attached. For a single location repair shop that was enough. There was no case for splitting it into more campaigns at this spend.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1100" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="27" name="Shape 23"/><p:cNvSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="713232" y="6053328"/><a:ext cx="10735056" cy="8230"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="E4E7EA"/></a:solidFill><a:ln w="12700"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="E4E7EA"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="28" name="Text 24"/><p:cNvSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="713232" y="6217920"/><a:ext cx="1005840" cy="237744"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" lIns="0" tIns="0" rIns="0" bIns="0" rtlCol="0" anchor="ctr"/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1000" i="1" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="8A929B"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Arial" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Arial" pitchFamily="34" charset="-122"/><a:cs typeface="Arial" pitchFamily="34" charset="-120"/></a:rPr><a:t>Looking back: </a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1000" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="29" name="Text 25"/><p:cNvSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="1673352" y="6199632"/><a:ext cx="9774936" cy="502920"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" lIns="0" tIns="0" rIns="0" bIns="0" rtlCol="0" anchor="ctr"/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPts val="1450"/></a:lnSpc><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1050" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="555D66"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Arial" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Arial" pitchFamily="34" charset="-122"/><a:cs typeface="Arial" pitchFamily="34" charset="-120"/></a:rPr><a:t>Calls are not the same as customers. I never got sight of how many turned into paid jobs. Next time I would ask for a simple intake log so we could work toward booked work instead of ringing phones.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1050" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>